Bharathi thaan avanga company-la biggest shareholder… aana avanga co-founder BK, just six months-la company-a vittu poitaaru. Still, company-la 50% shares avarukku sondham!

Starting-la rendu perum close friends. Company start pannumbodhu, Bharathi 50%, BK 50%. No conditions, no vesting agreement. Friendship-la ellame fair-ah dhaan irundhuchu.

Six months later, BK-ku big tech company-la job offer vandhuduchu. Avar company-a vittu poitaaru. Aana avaroda 50% shares mattum avar koodave irundhuduchu!

Ippo Bharathi dhaan customers handle panraanga, products build panraanga, company grow panraanga. Aana future-la varra profit-la half, work pannaadha BK-kum pogum. Idhukku peru **Dead Equity**.

Oru investor funding-ku varumbodhu cap table paarthuttu, 'Company-la work pannaadha person-kitta 50% equity irukka?' nu question kekkuraanga. Deal risk-la poiduchu!

Idha avoid panna, normally four-year vesting with one-year cliff use pannalaam. Six months-la leave pannina zero vested shares. 18 months work pannina, BK-oda original 50% grant-la roughly 37.5% vest aagum — company-la approximately 18.75%.

Innum AI inga help pannalaam! AI Governance Assistant use panni founder agreement, vesting clauses, IP ownership, cap table ellam analyse panni, potential red flags identify pannalaam. Aana final agreement lawyer review pannradhu essential.

Remember, friendship-la company start pannalaam. Aana company protect aaganumna agreements clear-ah irukkanum!


